WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.870
Watch one letter.

2
00:00:01.870 --> 00:00:05.240
«prendre», to take, gives you «il prend»,

3
00:00:05.240 --> 00:00:06.250
with a D.

4
00:00:06.250 --> 00:00:07.840
But «ils prennent»?

5
00:00:07.840 --> 00:00:11.150
The D vanishes, and an extra N appears.

6
00:00:11.150 --> 00:00:12.840
Now «écrire», to write.

7
00:00:12.840 --> 00:00:16.050
«j'écris». But «ils écrivent».

8
00:00:16.050 --> 00:00:18.020
Where did that V come from?

9
00:00:18.020 --> 00:00:20.730
So why is it «il prend» with a D,

10
00:00:20.730 --> 00:00:23.810
but «ils prennent» with a double N?

11
00:00:23.810 --> 00:00:27.230
In this mission, you'll
take «prendre» apart,

12
00:00:27.230 --> 00:00:28.840
one form at a time.

13
00:00:28.840 --> 00:00:32.510
Then you'll build singular forms
from stem and ending chips,

14
00:00:32.510 --> 00:00:34.200
one verb at a time.

15
00:00:34.200 --> 00:00:38.240
Your mission: work out
why «il prend» has a D,

16
00:00:38.240 --> 00:00:40.830
and «ils prennent» has a double N.
